From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:49:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] flow: AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR, where AUTO_MEMORIES' views are
 written and read
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Before, synthesis wrote AUTO_MEMORIES' generated views and lists into
$(RESULTS_DIR)/memories and every later stage read them from its own
RESULTS_DIR. A variant that runs stages on another variant's synthesis
(FLOW_INPUT_VARIANT) had no memories of its own, so load_stage_input
refused AUTO_MEMORIES=1 outright.

Now AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR names the directory, with an overridable default:

  export AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR ?= $(RESULTS_DIR)/memories

Synthesis writes there (gen_memories.py --out-dir, clean_synth), and
every reader goes through it: util.tcl's lists and views, synthesis's
inlined register files, regfile_dissolve.tcl, the KLayout technology's
LEFs and def2stream.py's blackbox list. With the default nothing
changes.

With FLOW_INPUT_VARIANT: a variant forked off another sets
AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR to that variant's memories for every stage it runs,
next to FLOW_INPUT_VARIANT=<variant> for the first one, and reads the
memories in place, nothing copied. load_stage_input now stops only when
AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR is still this variant's default, and says to set it.
A fork's klayout.lyt depends on the other variant's blackboxes.txt, not
on this variant's memories.json, so make does not regenerate memories
into a directory it only reads.

Carried in bazel-orfs for ORFS #4824 (AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR), on
0213 (#4812). One change beyond the upstream commit: regfile_place.tcl,
which only carried patches add, reads the register files' netlists and
placements through AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR too. Retires with the //:bump onto
an ORFS that has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
